  "final_answer": "I now have all the information I need from the Wikipedia page on the 2026 FIFA World Cup.\n\n## Answer\n\nThe most recent **FIFA World Cup** (men's) was the **2026 FIFA World Cup**.\n\n| Detail | Information |\n|---|---|\n| **When** | June 11 – July 19, 2026 |\n| **Where** | Co-hosted by **Canada, Mexico, and the United States** (16 cities: 11 in the U.S., 3 in Mexico, 2 in Canada) — the first World Cup hosted by three countries |\n| **Winner** | **Spain** (winning their 2nd title) |\n| **Runner-up** | Argentina (the defending champions) |\n\n### Final result\n**Spain defeated Argentina 1–0 after extra time** in the final, becoming the first team to hold both the men's and women's World Cup titles simultaneously (after Spain won the 2023 Women's World Cup). \n\n### Notable facts\n- The tournament was the first to feature **48 teams** (expanded from 32)\n- **Kylian Mbappé** (France) won the Golden Boot with 10 goals — his second consecutive\n- **Rodri** (Spain) won the Golden Ball (best player)\n- **Unai Simón** (Spain) won the Golden Glove (best goalkeeper)\n- **Pau Cubarsí** (Spain) won the Best Young Player award\n- Total attendance: nearly 7 million (highest in World Cup history)",
